---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import heroBg from '../assets/photographs/landscapes/hero-bg.jpg';
import nature01 from '../assets/photographs/nature/nature-01.jpg';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
---

<MainLayout
  title={`About the Photographer | ${siteConfig.brandName}`}
  description="The personal story, philosophy, and beginning photography journey of photo.pichi.ra — exploring wildlife, nature, rented gear, and post-processing."
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <!-- Header Hero -->
    <header class="about-hero">
      <div class="container-editorial">
        <span class="about-eyebrow">Personal Story</span>
        <h1 class="about-title">Hello, I'm behind photo.pichi.</h1>
        <p class="about-hero-lead">
          A personal journey of slowing down, observing the outdoors, and discovering beauty through the camera lens.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Visual Divider Frame -->
    <div class="container-editorial">
      <div class="about-feature-image-wrap">
        <Image
          src={heroBg}
          alt="Quiet landscape vista during morning mist"
          width={1400}
          height={750}
          format="webp"
          quality={88}
          loading="eager"
          class="about-feature-img"
        />
        <span class="feature-img-caption">Morning light over valley ridges • A study in stillness</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial Narrative -->
    <section class="about-narrative">
      <div class="container-editorial narrative-inner">
        <!-- Section: The Beginning -->
        <div class="narrative-block">
          <span class="block-tag">The Beginning</span>
          <h2 class="block-title">Two months into a lifelong curiosity</h2>
          <div class="block-prose">
            <p>
              I recently started this photography journey — roughly two months ago. There was no grand epiphany or formal masterclass; it simply started with a desire to spend more time outdoors and truly look at the living world around me.
            </p>
            <p>
              When you pick up a camera with intention, the ordinary transforms. You begin noticing how the first beam of morning sun warms the moss on tree bark, how quietly a bird perches before taking flight, and how animal expressions carry unmistakable character.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section: The Gear & Approach -->
        <div class="narrative-block">
          <span class="block-tag">Equipment &amp; Exploration</span>
          <h2 class="block-title">Rented gear &amp; open horizons</h2>
          <div class="block-prose">
            <p>
              I don't own an expensive camera kit. Instead, whenever I plan an outing to a park, woodland, or mountain trail, I rent a DSLR or mirrorless body along with different lenses.
            </p>
            <p>
              Renting has been an incredible way to learn. One weekend I might rent a telephoto lens to study skittish birds at a distance without disturbing their natural rhythms. Another weekend, I might try a prime lens for close-up foliage, dew drops, and earthy textures. Every outing is a fresh experiment in handling, framing, and learning how light behaves.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Callout Quote -->
        <div class="quote-callout">
          <blockquote>
            "Photography is about observation as much as it is about capturing an image. Sometimes it is a bird resting quietly, sometimes an animal in its natural habitat, or simply the way light falls across a landscape."
          </blockquote>
        </div>

        <!-- Section: The Digital Darkroom -->
        <div class="narrative-block">
          <span class="block-tag">The Digital Darkroom</span>
          <h2 class="block-title">Learning Lightroom &amp; Photoshop</h2>
          <div class="block-prose">
            <p>
              Capturing the RAW file in the field is only half the joy. Once back from a shoot, I spend hours learning post-processing inside Adobe Lightroom and studying Photoshop techniques.
            </p>
            <p>
              My goal in post-processing is never to create artificial, neon-saturated images. Instead, I focus on bringing out the authentic tones of nature — the rich deep greens of forest canopies, warm morning ochres, soft slate greys, and natural shadows. Learning how to shape contrast and color harmony is a skill I am practicing and refining with every new photograph.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Two-column visual and interest breakdown -->
        <div class="interests-grid">
          <div class="interest-col">
            <div class="interest-img-wrap">
              <Image
                src={nature01}
                alt="Intricate fern frond with morning dew drops"
                width={800}
                height={950}
                format="webp"
                quality={88}
                loading="lazy"
                class="interest-img"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="interest-col text-col">
            <span class="block-tag">Interests</span>
            <h3 class="interest-heading">Domains of Exploration</h3>
            <ul class="interest-list">
              <li>
                <strong>Wildlife:</strong> Documenting animals in their natural habitats with patience, respect, and non-intrusive observation.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Birds:</strong> Studying movement, flight patterns, and plumage in tree canopies, wetlands, and shores.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Nature:</strong> Finding beauty in micro-textures — dew drops, ferns, bark, lichen, and the forest floor.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Landscapes:</strong> Chasing sunrise, mountain horizons, open skies, and changing seasonal light.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Section: Follow the Journey -->
        <div class="narrative-block follow-block">
          <span class="block-tag">Continuous Learning</span>
          <h2 class="block-title">Follow along</h2>
          <div class="block-prose">
            <p>
              This website serves as my quiet digital exhibition and archive. As I take more weekend trips, rent new lenses, and continue learning Lightroom and Photoshop, new photographs will find their home here.
            </p>
            <p>
              If you appreciate the outdoors, nature photography, or watching a creative journey unfold from day one, you can follow me on Instagram:
            </p>
            <div class="about-action">
              <a
                href={siteConfig.instagram.url}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="btn btn-primary"
              >
                <span>Follow {siteConfig.instagram.handle} on Instagram</span>
                <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</MainLayout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    padding-top: var(--space-3xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-4xl);
    background-color: var(--bg-primary);
  }

  .about-hero {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .about-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-olive);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .about-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.2vw, 4.2rem);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .about-hero-lead {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1.6vw, 1.35rem);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .about-feature-image-wrap {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .about-feature-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    max-height: 520px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }

  .feature-img-caption {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .about-narrative {
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .narrative-inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .narrative-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .block-tag {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-forest);
  }

  .block-title {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.2vw, 2.5rem);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .block-prose {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .block-prose p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* Quote Callout */
  .quote-callout {
    padding: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-xl);
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-olive);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius-sm) var(--radius-sm) 0;
  }

  .quote-callout blockquote {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.2vw, 1.75rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Interests Grid */
  .interests-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    align-items: center;
    background-color: var(--bg-secondary);
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .interests-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.3fr;
      padding: var(--space-2xl);
    }
  }

  .interest-img-wrap {
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .interest-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .text-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .interest-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.85rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .interest-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .interest-list li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .interest-list li::before {
    content: '•';
    color: var(--accent-olive);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: -2px;
  }

  .interest-list strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .follow-block {
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .about-action {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }
</style>

